{"route":"/docs/4.0/getting-started/webpack/","version":"4.0","renderedVersion":"4.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Webpack","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn how to include Bootstrap in your project using Webpack 3."},"blocks":[{"id":"installing-bootstrap","type":"heading","en":"Installing Bootstrap","level":2},{"id":"installing-bootstrap--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/download/#npm\">Install bootstrap</a> as a Node.js module using npm."},{"id":"importing-javascript","type":"heading","en":"Importing JavaScript","level":2},{"id":"importing-javascript--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Import <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/javascript/\">Bootstrap’s JavaScript</a> by adding this line to your app’s entry point (usually <code>index.js</code> or <code>app.js</code>):"},{"id":"importing-javascript--code-1","type":"code","value":"import 'bootstrap';","language":"js"},{"id":"importing-javascript--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Alternatively, you may <strong>import plugins individually</strong> as needed:"},{"id":"importing-javascript--code-2","type":"code","value":"import 'bootstrap/js/dist/util';\nimport 'bootstrap/js/dist/dropdown';\n...","language":"js"},{"id":"importing-javascript--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap is dependent on <a href=\"https://jquery.com/\">jQuery</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/floating-ui/popper-docs/blob/main/docs/v1/index.md\">Popper</a>,\nthese are defined as <code>peerDependencies</code>, this means that you will have to make sure to add both of them\nto your <code>package.json</code> using <code>npm install --save jquery popper.js</code>."},{"id":"importing-javascript--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"importing-javascript--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Notice that if you chose to <strong>import plugins individually</strong>, you must also install <a href=\"https://github.com/webpack-contrib/exports-loader\">exports-loader</a>"}]},{"id":"importing-styles","type":"heading","en":"Importing Styles","level":2},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass","type":"heading","en":"Importing Precompiled Sass","level":3},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"To enjoy the full potential of Bootstrap and customize it to your needs, use the source files as a part of your project’s bundling process."},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"First, create your own <code>_custom.scss</code> and use it to override the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/options/\">built-in custom variables</a>. Then, use your main sass file to import your custom variables, followed by Bootstrap:"},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass--code-1","type":"code","value":"@import \"custom\";\n@import \"~bootstrap/scss/bootstrap\";","language":"scss"},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"For Bootstrap to compile, make sure you install and use the required loaders: <a href=\"https://github.com/webpack-contrib/sass-loader\">sass-loader</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/postcss/postcss-loader\">postcss-loader</a> with <a href=\"https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer#webpack\">Autoprefixer</a>. With minimal setup, your webpack config should include this rule or similar:"},{"id":"importing-precompiled-sass--code-2","type":"code","value":"  ...\n  {\n    test: /\\.(scss)$/,\n    use: [{\n      loader: 'style-loader', // inject CSS to page\n    }, {\n      loader: 'css-loader', // translates CSS into CommonJS modules\n    }, {\n      loader: 'postcss-loader', // Run post css actions\n      options: {\n        plugins: function () { // post css plugins, can be exported to postcss.config.js\n          return [\n            require('precss'),\n            require('autoprefixer')\n          ];\n        }\n      }\n    }, {\n      loader: 'sass-loader' // compiles Sass to CSS\n    }]\n  },\n  ...","language":"js"},{"id":"importing-compiled-css","type":"heading","en":"Importing Compiled CSS","level":3},{"id":"importing-compiled-css--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Alternatively, you may use Bootstrap’s ready-to-use css by simply adding this line to your project’s entry point:"},{"id":"importing-compiled-css--code-1","type":"code","value":"import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css';","language":"js"},{"id":"importing-compiled-css--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"In this case you may use your existing rule for <code>css</code> without any special modifications to webpack config except you don’t need <code>sass-loader</code> just <a href=\"https://github.com/webpack-contrib/style-loader\">style-loader</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/webpack-contrib/css-loader\">css-loader</a>."},{"id":"importing-compiled-css--code-2","type":"code","value":"  ...\n  module: {\n    rules: [\n      {\n        test: /\\.css$/,\n        use: ['style-loader', 'css-loader']\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  ...","language":"js"}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Theming","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/theming/"},{"en":"Build tools","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/build-tools/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.